449,"description":"Cleavage"},{"type":"Region","start":449,"end":575,"description":"Sufficient for dimerization of proICA512"},{"type":"Chain","start":449,"end":979,"description":"ICA512-transmembrane fragment"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":506,"end":506,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":524,"end":524,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":576,"end":600,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Region","start":601,"end":732,"description":"Sufficient for dimerization of proICA512"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":601,"end":979,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Chain","start":659,"end":979,"description":"ICA512-cleaved cytosolic fragment"},{"type":"Domain","start":709,"end":969,"description":"Tyrosine-protein phosphatase"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":754,"end":754,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO)"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homodimer; shown for the unprocessed protein (proICA512) in the endoplasmic reticulum and resolved during protein maturation as ICA512-TMF seems to be predominantly monomeric in secretory granules; however, ICA512-CCF interacts with ICA512-TMF disrupting the ICA512-TMF:SNTB2 complex. The isolated lumenal RESP18 homology domain has been shown to form disulfide-linked homooligomers (PubMed:18824546, PubMed:25561468, PubMed:26836020). Interacts (via cytoplasmic domain) with phosphorylated SNTB2; this protects PTPRN against cleavage by CAPN1 to produce ICA512-CCF. Dephosphorylation of SNTB2 upon insulin stimulation disrupts the interaction and results in PTPRN cleavage (PubMed:11483505). Interacts with SNX19 (PubMed:16273344). ICA512-CCF interacts with PIAS4; in the nucleus (PubMed:15596545). Interacts with STAT5B (phosphorylated); down-regulated by ICA512-CCF sumoylation; ICA512-CCF prevents STAT5B dephosphorylation; ICA512-CCF mediates interaction of STAT5B with PIAS4 (PubMed:15596545, PubMed:16622421). Interacts (via RESP18 homology domain) with insulin and pro-insulin (PubMed:26836020). Interacts with PTPRN2, PTPRA and PTPRE (By similarity)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q16849-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":950,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000409251.7"],"refseq":["NM_001199763.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001186692.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,478],[480,509,471]],"edits":[{"start":479,"end":508,"original":"KPLSLAAGVKLLEILAEHVHMSSGSFINIS","replacement":"N","added":1}],"missing":30,"replaced":0,"novel":1,"foldedAbsent":30,"foldedMissing":30,"features":[[3,30,0],[10,30,0],[11,30,0],[12,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q16849-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q16849-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":65.1,"plddt":[[0,12],[50,1],[0,1],[50,11],[0,9],[50,1],[70,2],[90,3],[70,21],[90,1],[70,2],[50,8],[70,10],[90,1],[70,1],[90,6],[70,2],[90,1],[70,4],[90,2],[70,2],[90,5],[70,9],[50,3],[0,65],[50,5],[0,142],[50,2],[70,1],[50,1],[70,10],[50,1],[70,1],[50,1],[70,17],[50,4],[0,47],[50,1],[0,51],[50,2],[70,10],[50,3],[70,45],[50,8],[0,7],[50,1],[70,8],[90,21],[70,9],[50,4],[0,8],[50,6],[70,6],[50,4],[0,46],[50,3],[70,15],[90,69],[70,6],[90,37],[70,1],[90,29],[70,1],[90,31],[70,2],[90,18],[70,3],[50,1],[70,2],[90,25],[70,10],[90,35],[70,5],[50,1],[0,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q16849-3","name":"3","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":889,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000423636.6"],"refseq":["NM_001199764.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001186693.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,91,889]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":90,"original":"MRRPRRPGGLGGSGGLRLLLCLLLLSSRPGGCSAVSAHGC","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":90,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":47,"foldedMissing":47,"features":[[0,34,0],[1,56,0],[2,56,0],[3,56,0],[4,1,0],[5,1,0],[6,2,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q16849-3-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q1